<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		The Big and Small EVA gene costs nine archite points when VRE - Starjack is installed, which is where the
		alternative vacuum resistance gene comes from.
		This folder only loads when Big and Small - Genes &amp; More is active (see loadFolders.xml), which is where the
		EVA gene is defined. The original also demanded Big and Small - Races; that check is dropped, because the gene
		is not a Races def and requiring Races would have skipped the change for anyone running Genes &amp; More alone.
		The mod gates sit on <li> nodes inside sequences, not on the <Operation> itself: RimWorld reads
		MayRequire only on list elements.

		Verified against Genes &amp; More 1.6: BS_EVA_Gene exists and has no biostatArc, so the add lands.

		Worth revisiting: the Convergence mod's Cherry Picker list retires BS_EVA_Gene when Starjack is installed,
		in which case this archite cost never applies. That list is opt-in, so the cost matters for anyone who
		leaves it unchecked.

	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationSequence">
		<operations>
			<li Class="PatchOperationSequence" MayRequire="vanillaracesexpanded.starjack">
				<operations>
					<li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
						<xpath>Defs/GeneDef[defName="BS_EVA_Gene"]</xpath>
						<value>
							<biostatArc>9</biostatArc>
						</value>
					</li>
				</operations>
			</li>
		</operations>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
